      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While procedural flaws can occur in any large system, major, credible evidence of widespread manipulation affecting election outcomes has not been substantiated by audits or court rulings. Concerns about signature mismatches and third-party collection are often addressed through varying state-specific verification rules and transparency measures. Ultimately, the system is designed with multiple redundancies, and ongoing post-election audits exist to independently verify these processes.",
